---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Scope, editorial method, sourcing policy, and contribution guide for the Bourdain Archive."
>
  <header class="page-intro about-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Method + scope · updated August 2026</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">About this archive</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Bourdain Archive is an independent, open-source finding aid for Anthony Bourdain’s work and
      cultural record. It exists to help people discover what he made, where he appeared, where he
      travelled, and where the underlying material can be found legally.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose-grid">
    <section>
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>
        Books, essays, field notes, television, films, voice and acting roles, podcasts, interviews,
        talks, primary web material, and substantial criticism or biography. “Substantial” means
        work with lasting documentary, literary, critical, or historical value—not recycled
        celebrity coverage.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>What this is not</h2>
      <p>
        This is not a mirror of copyrighted books, articles, transcripts, or episodes. It is not an
        official estate project, and it does not claim completeness where the evidence is still
        being reviewed.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>The three relationships</h2>
      <dl class="taxonomy-list">
        <div><dt>By Bourdain</dt><dd>Authored or co-authored work.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Featuring Bourdain</dt><dd>Interviews, performances, hosted work, and credited production roles.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>About Bourdain</dt><dd>Posthumous films, books, profiles, criticism, and reference material.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Evidence before certainty</h2>
      <p>
        Every canonical record should point to a publisher, broadcaster, archive, catalog, or
        reputable publication. Records marked <em>needs review</em> remain visible for research but
        are excluded from search-engine indexing until verified.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Images + rights</h2>
      <p>
        Covers and posters are used as a visual index and normally remain remote previews from
        publishers, libraries, broadcasters, or film databases. Local images require a recorded
        creator, source, license, and credit. The archive does not bulk-copy editorial photography.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Preserving the trail</h2>
      <p>
        Original URLs remain the primary citation. When a page disappears, the archive links to
        documented captures where available. Browse the <a href={withBase('/sources/')}>source ledger</a>
        to see the evidence behind the catalog.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="contribute-band">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections welcome</p>
    <h2>A public archive gets better in public.</h2>
    <p>
      Missing work, wrong episode order, a dead link, a stronger citation, or better rights-cleared
      artwork? Open an issue or pull request with the source that supports the change.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="primary-action" href="https://github.com/h0rv/bourdain-archive">Contribute on GitHub</a>
      <a href={withBase('/archive/')}>Browse the archive</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
